  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "Chef played an interesting game yesterday. This game is played with two variables XXX and YYY; initially, X=Y=0X = Y = 0X=Y=0. Chef may make an arbitrary number of moves (including zero). In each move, he must perform the following process:\n\n\nChoose any positive integer PPP such that P⋅P&gt;YP \\cdot P \\gt YP⋅P&gt;Y.\nChange XXX to PPP.\nAdd P⋅PP \\cdot PP⋅P to YYY.\nUnfortunately, Chef has a bad memory and he has forgotten the moves he made. He only remembers the value of XXX after the game finished; let's denote it by XfX_fXf​. Can you tell him the maximum possible number of moves he could have made in the game?",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤1051 \\le T \\le 10^51≤T≤105",
      "1≤Xf≤1091 \\le X_f \\le 10^91≤Xf​≤109"
    ],
    "inputFormat": "The first line of the input contains a single integer TTT denoting the number of test cases. The description of TTT test cases follows.\nThe first and only line of each test case contains a single integer XfX_fXf​.",
    "outputFormat": "For each test case, print a single line containing one integer — the maximum number of moves Chef could have made.",
    "notes": [],
    "sampleTestCases": [
      {
        "id": "sample_1",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "3\n3\n8\n9",
        "output": "3\n5\n6",
        "explanation": "Explanation:\nExample case 2: One possible sequence of values of XXX is 0→1→2→3→5→80 \\rightarrow 1 \\rightarrow 2 \\rightarrow 3 \\rightarrow 5 \\rightarrow 80→1→2→3→5→8."
      }
    ]
  },
